// Project-wide build variables, applied as the base configuration of the
// Xcode *project* so every target sees them — the app, the widget extension
// and the tests. Target-level xcconfigs (Debug/Release.xcconfig) and explicit
// target build settings still win over anything defined here.
//
// Flutter regenerates Generated.xcconfig on every `flutter build`/`flutter run`
// and it is not in version control. Including it here is what makes
// FLUTTER_BUILD_NAME/FLUTTER_BUILD_NUMBER readable from the widget extension,
// so the extension can never ship a version that disagrees with the app — App
// Store Connect rejects that. The include is optional so that opening the
// project in Xcode before any Flutter command still parses.
#include? "Generated.xcconfig"

// ── Apple identity ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// These are upstream ekaTimer's values, so a clean clone of this repository
// builds with upstream's identity and carries nobody's private signing setup.
//
// To build under your own identity, write Flutter/Identity.local.xcconfig next
// to this file and redefine any of the three. That file is not tracked (see
// ios/.gitignore); it is included last, so its values win:
//
//     APP_BUNDLE_ID = com.example.myapp
//     APP_GROUP_ID = group.com.example.myapp.shared
//     APP_DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = ABCDE12345
//
// APP_GROUP_ID is the container the app and the home-screen widget share, and
// APP_DEVELOPMENT_TEAM feeds DEVELOPMENT_TEAM for automatic signing. Both the
// bundle ID and the app group have to exist in the Apple Developer account that
// owns the team, so change all three together.
//
// CI writes Identity.local.xcconfig from a secret before building; see
// .github/workflows/ios-release.yml.
APP_BUNDLE_ID = org.ekatimer.ios.gmlpub
APP_GROUP_ID = group.org.ekatimer.ios.gmlpub.shared
APP_DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = UZ9CGUQ4RH

#include? "Identity.local.xcconfig"
